<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi offers two billion riyals in FRNs.</title>
<headline>Saudi offers two billion riyals in FRNs.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency (SAMA) has offered two billion riyals worth of five- and seven-year floating rate notes (FRNs), bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>SAMA, the kingdom's central bank, said it offered the FRN's to Saudi-based banks on Saturday.</p>
<p>The rate for five-year FRNs maturing on April 2, 2002 and worth one billion riyals were fixed on Monday at 6.18 percent.</p>
<p>The rate for seven-year FRNs maturing on April 2, 2004 and also worth one billion riyals were fixed at 6.28 percent.</p>
</text>
